@.str = private unnamed_addr constant [2278 x i8] c"Most commonly-used cvc5 options:\0A  --incremental | -i     enable incremental solving [*]\0A  --lang=LANG | --input-language=LANG | -L LANG\0A                         force input language (default is \22auto\22; see --lang\0A                         help)\0A  --output=TAG | -o TAG  Enable output tag.\0A  --parse-only           exit after parsing input [*]\0A  --preprocess-only      exit after preprocessing input [*]\0A  --quiet | -q           decrease verbosity (may be repeated)\0A  --rlimit=N             set resource limit\0A  --rlimit-per=N | --reproducible-resource-limit=N\0A                         set resource limit per query\0A  --safe-options         do not allow setting any option that is not common or\0A                         regular [*]\0A  --stats                give statistics on exit [*]\0A  --tlimit=MS            set time limit in milliseconds of wall clock time\0A  --tlimit-per=MS        set time limit per query in milliseconds\0A  --verbose | -v         increase verbosity (may be repeated)\0A  --verbosity=N          the verbosity level of cvc5\0A  --copyright            show cvc5 copyright information\0A  --help | -h            full command line reference\0A  --help-regular | -H    regular command line reference\0A  --interactive          force interactive shell/non-interactive mode [*]\0A  --print-success        print the \22success\22 output required of SMT-LIBv2 [*]\0A  --seed=N | -s N        seed for random number generator\0A  --show-config          show cvc5 static configuration\0A  --version | -V         identify this cvc5 binary\0A  --force-logic=LOGIC    set the logic, and override all further user attempts\0A                         to change it\0A  --strict-parsing       be less tolerant of non-conforming inputs [*]\0A  --dag-thresh=N         dagify common subexprs appearing > N times (1 ==\0A                         default, 0 == don't dagify)\0A  --output-lang=LANG | --output-language=LANG\0A                         force output language (default is \22auto\22; see\0A                         --output-lang help)\0A  --print-inst=MODE      print format for printing instantiations\0A  --check-models         after SAT/INVALID/UNKNOWN, check that the generated\0A                         model satisfies user assertions [*]\0A  --produce-models | -m  support the get-value and get-model commands [*]\0A\00", align 1
@_ZN4cvc54mainL28additionalOptionsDescriptionB5cxx11E = internal global %"class.std::__cxx11::basic_string" zeroinitializer, align 8
@.str.3 = private unnamed_addr constant [58056 x i8] c"Additional cvc5 options:\0A\0AFrom the Arithmetic Theory module:\0A  --approx-branch-depth=N\0A                         maximum branch depth the approximate solver is allowed\0A                         to take (EXPERTS only)\0A  --arith-brab           whether to use simple rounding, similar to a unit-cube\0A                         test, for integers [*]\0A  --arith-eq-solver      whether to use the equality solver in the theory of\0A                         arithmetic (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --arith-no-partial-fun do not use partial function semantics for arithmetic\0A                         (not SMT LIB compliant) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --arith-prop=MODE      turns on arithmetic propagation (default is 'old', see\0A                         --arith-prop=help) (EXPERTS only)\0A  --arith-prop-clauses=N rows shorter than this are propagated as clauses\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --arith-rewrite-equalities\0A                         turns on the preprocessing rewrite turning equalities\0A                         into a conjunction of inequalities [*]\0A  --arith-static-learning\0A                         do arithmetic static learning for ite terms based on\0A                         bounds when static learning is enabled [*]\0A  --collect-pivot-stats  collect the pivot history (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --cut-all-bounded      turns on the integer solving step of periodically\0A                         cutting all integer variables that have both upper and\0A                         lower bounds (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dio-decomps          let skolem variables for integer divisibility\0A                         constraints leak from the dio solver (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dio-solver           turns on Linear Diophantine Equation solver (Griggio,\0A                         JSAT 2012) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dio-turns=N          turns in a row dio solver cutting gets (EXPERTS only)\0A  --error-selection-rule=RULE\0A                         change the pivot rule for the basic variable (default\0A                         is 'min', see --pivot-rule help) (EXPERTS only)\0A  --fc-penalties         turns on degenerate pivot penalties (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --heuristic-pivots=N   the number of times to apply the heuristic pivot rule;\0A                         if N < 0, this defaults to the number of variables; if\0A                         this is unset, this is tuned by the logic selection\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --lemmas-on-replay-failure\0A                         attempt to use external lemmas if approximate solve\0A                         integer failed (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --maxCutsInContext=N   maximum cuts in a given context before signalling a\0A                         restart (EXPERTS only)\0A  --miplib-trick         turns on the preprocessing step of attempting to infer\0A                         bounds on miplib problems (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --miplib-trick-subs=N  do substitution for miplib 'tmp' vars if defined in <=\0A                         N eliminated vars (EXPERTS only)\0A  --new-prop             use the new row propagation system (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --nl-cov               whether to use the cylindrical algebraic coverings\0A                         solver for non-linear arithmetic [*]\0A  --nl-cov-force         forces using the cylindrical algebraic coverings\0A                         solver, even in cases where it is possibly not safe to\0A                         do so (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --nl-cov-lift=MODE     choose the Coverings lifting mode (EXPERTS only)\0A  --nl-cov-linear-model=MODE\0A                         whether to use the linear model as initial guess for\0A                         the cylindrical algebraic coverings solver\0A  --nl-cov-proj=MODE     choose the Coverings projection operator (EXPERTS only)\0A  --nl-cov-prune         whether to prune intervals more agressively (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --nl-cov-var-elim      whether to eliminate variables using equalities before\0A                         going into the cylindrical algebraic coverings solver.\0A                         It can not be used when producing proofs right now.\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --nl-ext=MODE          incremental linearization approach to non-linear\0A  --nl-ext-ent-conf      check for entailed conflicts in non-linear solver\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --nl-ext-factor        use factoring inference in non-linear incremental\0A                         linearization solver [*]\0A  --nl-ext-inc-prec      whether to increment the precision for irrational\0A                         function constraints (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --nl-ext-purify        purify non-linear terms at preprocess (EXPERTS only)\0A                         [*]\0A  --nl-ext-rbound        use resolution-style inference for inferring new bounds\0A                         in non-linear incremental linearization solver (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --nl-ext-rewrite       do context-dependent simplification based on rewrites\0A                         in non-linear solver [*]\0A  --nl-ext-split-zero    initial splits on zero for all variables (EXPERTS only)\0A                         [*]\0A  --nl-ext-tf-taylor-deg=N\0A                         initial degree of polynomials for Taylor approximation\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --nl-ext-tf-tplanes    use non-terminating tangent plane strategy for\0A                         transcendental functions for non-linear incremental\0A                         linearization solver [*]\0A  --nl-ext-tplanes       use non-terminating tangent plane strategy for\0A                         non-linear incremental linearization solver [*]\0A  --nl-ext-tplanes-interleave\0A                         interleave tangent plane strategy for non-linear\0A                         incremental linearization solver [*]\0A  --nl-icp               whether to use ICP-style propagations for non-linear\0A                         arithmetic (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --nl-rlv=MODE          choose mode for using relevance of assertions in\0A                         non-linear arithmetic (EXPERTS only)\0A  --nl-rlv-assert-bounds use bound inference utility to prune when an assertion\0A                         is entailed by another (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --pb-rewrites          apply pseudo boolean rewrites (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --pivot-threshold=N    sets the number of pivots using --pivot-rule per basic\0A                         variable per simplex instance before using variable\0A                         order (EXPERTS only)\0A  --pp-assert-max-sub-size=N\0A                         threshold for substituting an equality in ppAssert\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --prop-row-length=N    sets the maximum row length to be used in propagation\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --replay-early-close-depth=N\0A                         multiples of the depths to try to close the approx log\0A                         eagerly (EXPERTS only)\0A  --replay-lemma-reject-cut=N\0A                         maximum complexity of any coefficient while outputting\0A                         replaying cut lemmas (EXPERTS only)\0A  --replay-num-err-penalty=N\0A                         number of solve integer attempts to skips after a\0A                         numeric failure (EXPERTS only)\0A  --replay-reject-cut=N  maximum complexity of any coefficient while replaying\0A                         cuts (EXPERTS only)\0A  --restrict-pivots      have a pivot cap for simplex at effort levels below\0A                         fullEffort (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --revert-arith-models-on-unsat\0A                         revert the arithmetic model to a known safe model on\0A                         unsat if one is cached (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --rr-turns=N           round robin turn (EXPERTS only)\0A  --se-solve-int         attempt to use the approximate solve integer method on\0A                         standard effort (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --simplex-check-period=N\0A                         the number of pivots to do in simplex before rechecking\0A                         for a conflict on all variables (EXPERTS only)\0A  --soi-qe               use quick explain to minimize the sum of infeasibility\0A                         conflicts (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --standard-effort-variable-order-pivots=N\0A                         limits the number of pivots in a single invocation of\0A                         check() at a non-full effort level using Bland's pivot\0A                         rule (EXPERTS only)\0A  --unate-lemmas=MODE    determines which lemmas to add before solving (default\0A                         is 'all', see --unate-lemmas=help) (EXPERTS only)\0A  --use-approx           attempt to use an approximate solver (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --use-fcsimplex        use focusing and converging simplex (FMCAD 2013\0A                         submission) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --use-soi              use sum of infeasibility simplex (FMCAD 2013\0A                         submission) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Arrays Theory module:\0A  --arrays-eager-index   turn on eager index splitting for generated array\0A                         lemmas [*]\0A  --arrays-eager-lemmas  turn on eager lemma generation for arrays (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --arrays-exp           enable experimental features in the theory of arrays\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --arrays-optimize-linear\0A                         turn on optimization for linear array terms (see de\0A                         Moura FMCAD 09 arrays paper) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --arrays-prop=N        propagation effort for arrays: 0 is none, 1 is some, 2\0A                         is full (EXPERTS only)\0A  --arrays-reduce-sharing\0A                         use model information to reduce size of care graph for\0A                         arrays (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --arrays-weak-equiv    use algorithm from Christ/Hoenicke (SMT 2014) (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Base module:\0A  --err=erroutput | --diagnostic-output-channel=erroutput\0A                         Set the error (or diagnostic) output channel. Writes to\0A                         stderr for \22stderr\22 or \22--\22, stdout for \22stdout\22 or the\0A                         given filename otherwise. (EXPERTS only)\0A  --in=input             Set the error (or diagnostic) output channel. Reads\0A                         from stdin for \22stdin\22 or \22--\22 and the given filename\0A                         otherwise. (EXPERTS only)\0A  --out=output | --regular-output-channel=output\0A                         Set the error (or diagnostic) output channel. Writes to\0A                         stdout for \22stdout\22 or \22--\22, stderr for \22stderr\22 or the\0A                         given filename otherwise. (EXPERTS only)\0A  --rweight=VAL=N        set a single resource weight (EXPERTS only)\0A  --stats-all            print unchanged (defaulted) statistics as well (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --stats-every-query    in incremental mode, print stats after every\0A                         satisfiability or validity query [*]\0A  --stats-internal       print internal (non-public) statistics as well (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --trace=TAG | -t TAG   trace something (e.g. -t pushpop), can repeat and may\0A                         contain wildcards like (e.g. -t theory::*)\0A\0AFrom the Bitvector Theory module:\0A  --bitblast=MODE        choose bitblasting mode, see --bitblast=help\0A  --bitwise-eq           lift equivalence with one-bit bit-vectors to be boolean\0A                         operations [*]\0A  --bool-to-bv=MODE      convert booleans to bit-vectors of size 1 at various\0A                         levels of aggressiveness, see --bool-to-bv=help\0A  --bv-assert-input      assert input assertions on user-level 0 instead of\0A                         assuming them in the bit-vector SAT solver (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --bv-eager-eval        perform eager context-dependent evaluation for\0A                         applications of bv kinds in the equality engine [*]\0A  --bv-eq-engine         enable equality engine when possible in bitvector\0A                         theory (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --bv-gauss-elim        simplify formula via Gaussian Elimination if applicable\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --bv-intro-pow2        introduce bitvector powers of two as a preprocessing\0A                         pass (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --bv-propagate         use bit-vector propagation in the bit-blaster (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --bv-rw-extend-eq      enable additional rewrites over zero/sign extend over\0A                         equalities with constants (useful on\0A                         BV/2017-Preiner-scholl-smt08) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --bv-sat-solver=MODE   choose which sat solver to use, see\0A                         --bv-sat-solver=help\0A  --bv-solver=MODE       choose bit-vector solver, see --bv-solver=help\0A  --bv-to-bool           lift bit-vectors of size 1 to booleans when possible\0A                         [*]\0A\0AFrom the Datatypes Theory module:\0A  --cdt-bisimilar        do bisimilarity check for co-datatypes (EXPERTS only)\0A                         [*]\0A  --dt-binary-split      do binary splits for datatype constructor types\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dt-blast-splits      when applicable, blast splitting lemmas for all\0A                         variables at once (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dt-cyclic            do cyclicity check for datatypes (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dt-infer-as-lemmas   always send lemmas out instead of making internal\0A                         inferences (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dt-nested-rec        allow nested recursion in datatype definitions (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --dt-polite-optimize   turn on optimization for polite combination (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --dt-share-sel         internally use shared selectors across multiple\0A                         constructors [*]\0A  --sygus-abort-size=N   tells enumerative sygus to only consider solutions up\0A                         to term size N (-1 == no limit, default)\0A  --sygus-fair=MODE      if and how to apply fairness for sygus\0A  --sygus-fair-max       use max instead of sum for multi-function sygus\0A                         conjectures (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --sygus-rewriter=MODE  if and how to apply rewriting for sygus symmetry\0A                         breaking\0A  --sygus-simple-sym-break=MODE\0A                         if and how to apply simple symmetry breaking based on\0A                         the grammar for smart enumeration\0A  --sygus-sym-break-lazy lazily add symmetry breaking lemmas for terms (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --sygus-sym-break-pbe  sygus symmetry breaking lemmas based on pbe conjectures\0A                         [*]\0A  --sygus-sym-break-rlv  add relevancy conditions to symmetry breaking lemmas\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Decision Heuristics module:\0A  --decision=MODE | --decision-mode=MODE\0A                         choose decision mode, see --decision=help\0A  --jh-rlv-order         maintain activity-based ordering for decision\0A                         justification heuristic (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --jh-skolem=MODE       policy for when to satisfy skolem definitions in\0A                         justification heuristic (EXPERTS only)\0A  --jh-skolem-rlv=MODE   policy for when to consider skolem definitions relevant\0A                         in justification heuristic (EXPERTS only)\0A\0AFrom the Expression module:\0A  --type-checking        type check expressions (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --wf-checking          check that terms passed to API methods are well formed\0A                         (default false for text interface) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Finite Field Theory module:\0A  --ff-field-polys       include field polynomials in Groebner basis\0A                         computation; don't do this (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --ff-trace-gb          use a traced groebner basis engine (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Floating-Point module:\0A  --fp-exp               Allow floating-point sorts of all sizes, rather than\0A                         only Float32 (8/24) or Float64 (11/53) (experimental)\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --fp-lazy-wb           Enable lazier word-blasting (on preNotifyFact instead\0A                         of registerTerm) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Driver module:\0A  --dump-difficulty      dump the difficulty measure after every response to\0A                         check-sat [*]\0A  --dump-instantiations  output instantiations of quantified formulas after\0A                         every UNSAT/VALID response [*]\0A  --dump-instantiations-debug\0A                         output instantiations of quantified formulas after\0A                         every UNSAT/VALID response, with debug information\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --dump-models          output models after every SAT/INVALID/UNKNOWN response\0A                         [*]\0A  --dump-proofs          output proofs after every UNSAT/VALID response [*]\0A  --dump-unsat-cores     output unsat cores after every UNSAT/VALID response [*]\0A  --early-exit           do not run destructors at exit; default on except in\0A                         debug builds (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --force-no-limit-cpu-while-dump\0A                         Force no CPU limit when dumping models and proofs\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --portfolio-jobs=n     Number of parallel jobs the portfolio engine can run\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --segv-spin            spin on segfault/other crash waiting for gdb (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --show-trace-tags      show all available tags for tracing (EXPERTS only)\0A  --stdin-input-per-line when piping from stdin, feed the input to the parser\0A                         one line at a time. (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --use-portfolio        Use internal portfolio mode based on the logic (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Parallel module:\0A  --append-learned-literals-to-cubes\0A                         emit learned literals with the cubes (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --checks-before-partition=N\0A                         number of standard or full effort checks until\0A                         partitioning (EXPERTS only)\0A  --checks-between-partitions=N\0A                         number of checks between partitions (EXPERTS only)\0A  --compute-partitions=N make n partitions. n <2 disables computing partitions\0A                         entirely (EXPERTS only)\0A  --partition-check=MODE | --check=MODE\0A                         select whether partitioning happens at full or standard\0A                         check (EXPERTS only)\0A  --partition-conflict-size=N\0A                         number of literals in a cube; if no partition size is\0A                         set, then the partition conflict size is chosen to be\0A                         log2(number of requested partitions) (EXPERTS only)\0A  --partition-start-time=N\0A                         time to start creating partitions in seconds (EXPERTS\0A                         only)\0A  --partition-strategy=MODE | --partition=MODE\0A                         choose partition strategy mode (EXPERTS only)\0A  --partition-time-interval=N\0A                         time to wait between scatter partitions (EXPERTS only)\0A  --partition-tlimit=N   time limit for partitioning in seconds (EXPERTS only)\0A  --partition-when=MODE  choose when to partition (EXPERTS only)\0A  --random-partitioning  create random partitions (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --write-partitions-to=output | --partitions-out=output\0A                         set the output channel for writing partitions (EXPERTS\0A                         only)\0A\0AFrom the Parser module:\0A  --filesystem-access    limits the file system access if set to false (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --fresh-declarations   use API interface for fresh constants when parsing\0A                         declarations and definitions [*]\0A  --global-declarations  force all declarations and definitions to be global\0A                         when parsing [*]\0A  --semantic-checks      enable semantic checks, including type checks (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Printing module:\0A  --bv-print-consts-as-indexed-symbols\0A                         print bit-vector constants in decimal (e.g. (_ bv1 4))\0A                         instead of binary (e.g. #b0001), applies to SMT-LIB 2.x\0A                         [*]\0A  --expr-depth=N         print exprs to depth N (0 == default, -1 == no limit)\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --flatten-ho-chains    print (binary) application chains in a flattened way,\0A                         e.g. (a b c) rather than ((a b) c) (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --model-u-print=MODE   determines how to print uninterpreted elements in\0A                         models\0A\0AFrom the Proof module:\0A  --alf-print-reference  Print reference to original file instead of redeclaring\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --check-proof-steps    Check proof steps for satisfiability, for refutation\0A                         soundness testing. Note this checks only steps for\0A                         non-core proof rules (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --lfsc-expand-trust    Print the children of trusted proof steps (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --lfsc-flatten         Flatten steps in the LFSC proof (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --opt-res-reconstruction-size\0A                         Optimize resolution reconstruction to reduce proof size\0A                         [*]\0A  --print-dot-clusters   Whether the proof node clusters (e.g. SAT, CNF, INPUT)\0A                         will be printed when using the dot format or not. [*]\0A  --proof-alethe-res-pivots\0A                         Add pivots to Alethe resolution steps (EXPERTS only)\0A                         [*]\0A  --proof-annotate       add optional annotations to proofs, which enables\0A                         statistics for inference ids for lemmas and conflicts\0A                         appearing in final proof (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --proof-check=MODE     select internal proof checking mode (EXPERTS only)\0A  --proof-dot-dag        Indicates if the dot proof will be printed as a DAG or\0A                         as a tree (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --proof-format-mode=MODE\0A                         select language of proof output\0A  --proof-granularity=MODE\0A                         modes for proof granularity\0A  --proof-pedantic=N     assertion failure for any incorrect rule application or\0A                         untrusted lemma having pedantic level <=N with proof\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --proof-pp-merge       merge subproofs in final proof post-processor (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A  --proof-print-conclusion\0A                         Print conclusion of proof steps when printing AST\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --proof-prune-input    Prune unused input assumptions from final scope\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --proof-rewrite-rcons-limit=N\0A                         the matching recursion limit for reconstructing proofs\0A                         of theory rewrites\0A\0AFrom the