n for finding conflicts\0A                         and avoiding regular expression unfolding [*]\0A  --strings-rexplain-lemmas\0A                         regression explanations for string lemmas (EXPERTS\0A                         only) [*]\0A\0AFrom the Theory Layer module:\0A  --assign-function-values\0A                         assign values for uninterpreted functions in models\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --condense-function-values\0A                         condense values for functions in models rather than\0A                         explicitly representing them (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --ee-mode=MODE         mode for managing equalities across theory solvers\0A                         (EXPERTS only)\0A  --relevance-filter     enable analysis of relevance of asserted literals with\0A                         respect to the input formula (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --tc-mode=MODE         mode for theory combination (EXPERTS only)\0A  --theoryof-mode=MODE   mode for Theory::theoryof() (EXPERTS only)\0A\0AFrom the Uninterpreted Functions Theory module:\0A  --eager-arith-bv-conv  eagerly expand bit-vector to arithmetic conversions\0A                         during preprocessing (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --symmetry-breaker     use UF symmetry breaker (Deharbe et al., CADE 2011)\0A                         (EXPERTS only) [*]\0A  --uf-ho-ext            apply extensionality on function symbols (EXPERTS only)\0A                         [*]\0A  --uf-lazy-ll           do lambda lifting lazily [*]\0A  --uf-ss=MODE           mode of operation for uf with cardinality solver.\0A  --uf-ss-abort-card=N   tells the uf with cardinality to only consider models\0A                         that interpret uninterpreted sorts of cardinality at\0A                         most N (-1 == no limit, default)\0A  --uf-ss-fair           use fair strategy for finite model finding multiple\0A                         sorts [*]\0A  --uf-ss-fair-monotone  group monotone sorts when enforc